## User preferences

- voice “should just be using byok instead” and “there should be no browser voice used as that is terrible for the quality” -> use the selected Voice Narration provider/model or surface its error, never silently switch [Task 1]
- the user wanted editors to “respond to me as I draft directly,” address the writer personally, and retain personal facts/feedback preferences -> make writer context first-class settings and send it through the shared persona prompt [Task 1]
- when the user asked for voice icons “in the modals that pop up in the editor for each passage” -> wire polished speak controls across relevant passage popovers/modals [Task 1]
- “I would like the responses streamed rather than just waiting all at once for the text” -> show cumulative visible text, reset on retry, and keep reasoning separate [Task 2]
- “there is a dossier per folio” -> default to independent optional folio scope, not an account singleton [Task 3]

## Reusable knowledge

- `resolveFeatureConfig(settings, "voice-narration")` honors `perFeature["voice-narration"]`; cache identity must include provider, model, voice, and text. `saveAiSettingsToIdb` emits `twyne:ai-settings-saved`, which invalidates orchestrator settings cache [Task 1]
- Tinker browser requests fail CORS. Use the constrained same-origin endpoints `/api/tinker/models` and `/api/tinker/chat/completions`; only route audio-capable models direct `input_audio`, convert recordings to WAV when needed, and never persist/log keys [Task 1]
- Client streaming choke point is `runOnce` -> `generateTrackedText` -> public `runClient*`. Qwik interview streaming consumes `streamText().fullStream` `text-delta`/`reasoning-delta`, withholding partial `<think>` and `DOSSIER`/`PROBE`/`SYNTHESIZE` payloads [Task 2]
- Per-folio migration spans IDB folio-keyed brief helpers, legacy mirrors, active-folio routes, `(userId, folioId)` Convex indexing, and bulk sync. Migrate a legacy global dossier only if no folio dossier exists [Task 3]

